      "description": "Merges head (with its first-parent chain since base) three-way onto target, main by default, and publishes the result as one changeset in one transaction; on E_CONFLICT, details.report lists each conflict: resolve them with resolutions, against the report's theirs, its full 64-hex id (a path the target changed since comes back in the report's stale). Give idempotency_key to make a retry safe.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "description": "`land`: merge a change three-way onto a target ref and publish it there as one new\nchangeset, in one transaction (operations spec §3). The change is `head` with its\nfirst-parent chain after `base`, squashed: the landed changeset's parent is the target's\nhead, so the target stays linear. A conflict is the error `E_CONFLICT`, with the report in\n`details.report`; nothing is recorded then.",
        "properties": {
          "base": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "description": "A revision as the caller wrote it, for the store to resolve: a ref name (`main`,\n`release/1.2`), a full 64-hex changeset id or a unique prefix of at least 12 hex digits,\noptionally followed by `~N` for the N-th first-parent ancestor.",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Where the change starts: a first-parent ancestor of `head`, whose own changes are not part\nof it (anything else is `E_INVALID_ARG`). It need not be on the target. When omitted, the\nmerge base of `head` and the target's head, along first parents."
          },
          "expect_target": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "pattern": "^[0-9a-fA-F]{64}$",
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Publish only while the target names this changeset (M5): one attempt, and a target that\nnames another is `E_CAS_MISMATCH`, nothing written; `max_attempts` does not apply. With a\n`head` rebased onto it, the landed tree is the rebased tree. `swarmops mcp` refuses one\nthat is not a full 64-hex id (`E_INVALID_ARG`)."
          },
          "head": {
            "description": "The changeset to land: the change's head. A revision as the caller wrote it, for the store to resolve: a ref name (`main`,\n`release/1.2`), a full 64-hex changeset id or a unique prefix of at least 12 hex digits,\noptionally followed by `~N` for the N-th first-parent ancestor.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "idempotency_key": {
            "description": "Makes a retry of this land safe: 1 to 64 letters, digits and `-`, such as a uuid v7. A land\nwith a key first looks down the target's first parents, to `base`, for a changeset that\nlanded with the same key: one squashed from this `head` is the replay, which writes\nnothing (`status` is `replayed`); one from another head is `E_INVALID_ARG`, a key used\nfor another change.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "max_attempts": {
            "default": 8,
            "description": "How many times to try to publish before failing with `E_CAS_RETRY_EXHAUSTED`: 1 to 32.",
            "format": "uint32",
            "maximum": 32,
            "minimum": 1,
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "max_conflict_bytes": {
            "default": 32768,
            "description": "The most bytes of hunk text an `E_CONFLICT` report carries: from the first hunk whose\ntexts would pass it, no hunk carries its texts (`truncated`), and the hunks' line\npositions and the blob ids stay. The report's files are bounded apart from it, as\n`ConflictReport.files` says.",
            "format": "uint64",
            "minimum": 0,
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "message": {
            "description": "The landed changeset's message; `head`'s when omitted.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "resolutions": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "description": "A land's resolutions (`land --resolve`): what to make of some paths of the merge of the change\nonto the target, decided against one of the target's heads.",
                "properties": {
                  "against": {
                    "description": "The target's head the resolutions were decided against: the conflict report's `theirs`,\nby its full 64-hex id. A resolution applies while the target holds its path as this\nchangeset does (the same file, the same directory, or nothing). A revision as the caller wrote it, for the store to resolve: a ref name (`main`,\n`release/1.2`), a full 64-hex changeset id or a unique prefix of at least 12 hex digits,\noptionally followed by `~N` for the N-th first-parent ancestor.",
                    "type": "string"
