      },
      "description": "Sends a store ref (main by default) to a git remote's branch by compare-and-swap, never by force: the remote moves only from what the last fetch saw. A remote that moved since is E_REMOTE_DIVERGED and nothing is sent: fetch or sync, then push again. Run again, it sends nothing.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "description": "`push`: send a store ref to a remote branch by compare-and-swap, never forcing: the remote\nmoves only from the head the last fetch saw to a descendant of it. A push is an export, so\nit needs no identity.",
        "properties": {
          "branch": {
            "description": "The remote branch; by default the remote's followed branch for `main`, and the same\nname for `release/<name>`.",
            "type": [
              "string",
